WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:03.630
- So what advice would I have for someone

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:06.340
who wants to be an entrepreneur?

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:07.920
So everyone's path is different,

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.210
so take anything I have to say

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:10.440
with a grain of salt.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.167
But a lot of folks think
of entrepreneurship as,

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:15.060
"Hey, I have a new idea for a business,"

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:18.070
whether it's a restaurant,
or a new technology company,

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:19.770
a new social network,
whatever it might be,

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:23.080
and they put a lot of
emphasis on the idea itself.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.090
And I think most
entrepreneurs would tell you

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:27.840
that a lot more depends
not only on the idea

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.110
but the execution of the idea,

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:31.620
and really just how ready is the world,

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:34.080
is the market, for your idea?

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.650
And so my advice would be, especially

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:38.740
if you're early in your career,

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:40.780
try to build as many skills as you can,

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:42.098
and to be an entrepreneur,

00:00:42.098 --> 00:00:44.390
you have to be a little bit
of a jack of all trades.

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:45.620
So know your finance.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:46.453
Know your accounting.

00:00:46.453 --> 00:00:47.520
Know your marketing,

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.690
And you don't have to know
it necessarily academically,

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:50.640
but know it intuitively.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.834
Pay attention to how
other people are doing it.

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:54.950
Think about your strategy.

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:58.100
And wherever your area of interest is,

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.550
if it's to start a restaurant,

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.110
get to know that business
really, really, really well.

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:04.280
Work at a restaurant at all levels.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:06.200
If your goal is to work in tech,

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:07.370
work at some tech companies.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:08.665
Get to know that really, really well.

00:01:08.665 --> 00:01:10.660
Get to know not just the technology,

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:11.850
not just the product management,

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:14.490
not just the design, but
the sales aspect of it.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:16.800
Get to know the management aspect of it.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.730
And the whole time that
you're building yourself up,

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:20.960
that you're working in
industry and learning

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.090
these various skills,
make sure that you have

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:24.127
some time to fiddle.

00:01:24.127 --> 00:01:27.660
The best entrepreneurial ideas
that I've seen are the ones

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:30.150
where folks get to know a space well

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:32.820
through their craft, and
then they have an idea,

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.330
and then they're able to have a little bit

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:35.890
of time to test out that idea,

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:37.772
not only build it, not only prototype it,

00:01:37.772 --> 00:01:39.530
but put it out there somehow

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:40.910
and see how it the market responds.

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:42.930
And if the market is
responding very favorably,

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:44.711
if people are saying,
"Wow, I want more of this.

00:01:44.711 --> 00:01:45.952
"How can I get it?"

00:01:45.952 --> 00:01:47.774
Then I think you're on to something.

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:50.410
And all of those skills
that you would have built up

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.850
over those many years,
not only will they help

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:53.996
you execute on the idea,

00:01:53.996 --> 00:01:56.490
but they'll help you convince other people

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:58.460
that you're ready to execute on the idea,

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:00.080
which is maybe just as important,

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.120
potential investors, people that you need

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:04.704
to co-found your venture with,

00:02:04.704 --> 00:02:08.210
and also, my last point is
know what your weak points are.

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:10.053
As you experience all of these dimensions

00:02:10.053 --> 00:02:12.860
of starting a business, if you know that,

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:15.600
hey maybe the marketing
isn't my thing, know that.

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.392
And then you could find
someone who's good at it,

00:02:17.392 --> 00:02:19.407
who can complement you, if you're like,

00:02:19.407 --> 00:02:21.157
"Hey, I like the entrepreneurial side,

00:02:21.157 --> 00:02:23.737
"but scaling up a business
isn't my cup of tea."

00:02:23.737 --> 00:02:26.420
Find great operators who
can help you scale it up.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:28.010
So that's my two cents.

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:29.660
Take it all with a grain of salt.

